direction: down

title: |md
  ### Helpers vs kfuncs (language level)
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

helper: "Calling a helper" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
  h_body: |md
    ```c
    #include <bpf/bpf_helpers.h>

    /* header declares it as a fn-pointer
       constant at a fixed enum offset:
       (void *)BPF_FUNC_map_lookup_elem */
    void *p =
      bpf_map_lookup_elem(&map, &key);
    ```
    - Frozen UAPI list (≈230 entries)
    - Compiles to a `call` with immediate = enum value
    - Verifier reads proto from `bpf_func_proto`
  |
}

kfunc: "Calling a kfunc" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  k_body: |md
    ```c
    extern struct task_struct *
    bpf_task_acquire(
      struct task_struct *) __ksym;

    extern void
    bpf_task_release(
      struct task_struct *) __ksym;

    struct task_struct *t =
      bpf_task_acquire(cur);
    if (!t) return 0;
    /* ... */
    bpf_task_release(t);
    ```
    - In-tree, NOT frozen UAPI
    - Compiled as ordinary symbol refs
    - Resolved vs kernel BTF at load
    - Verifier checks proto from BTF
    - Lifetime enforced (acquire/release)
  |
}

verdict: |md
  - **New BPF features arrive as kfuncs.**
  - Helpers stop growing; the existing list stays frozen.
  - Wherever you see `__ksym`, that's a kfunc.
| {near: bottom-center; shape: text}

helper -> kfunc -> verdict
